---
import ToolPageLayout from "../../layouts/ToolPageLayout.astro";
import ServiceEstimateCalculator from "../../components/calculator/ServiceEstimateCalculator";

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How is an estimate calculator different from a cost calculator?",
    answer:
      "The cost calculator starts with category totals. This worksheet builds a project from service quantities and direct costs per unit, then adds shared expenses, overhead, and margin.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I calculate more than one project at a time?",
    answer:
      "The free version calculates one project. Landscape Estimate Pro saves unlimited projects and estimates, plus reusable service assemblies so you don't re-enter the same materials and labor every time.",
  },
  {
    question: "Does it factor in my production rates?",
    answer:
      "This worksheet takes a direct unit cost you have already worked out for each service, including labor. Pro adds production-rate labor calculation — enter a quantity (e.g. 8 yd³ of mulch) and your own production rate (e.g. 2.5 yd³ per person-hour), and it calculates person-hours and labor cost for you.",
  },
  {
    question: "What's the difference between required price and display price?",
    answer:
      "This worksheet rounds true cost to cents, then rounds the required selling price upward to the next cent. It does not round down or automatically choose a whole-dollar customer quote.",
  },
];
---

<ToolPageLayout
  title="Landscaping Estimate Calculator — Multi-Service Worksheet"
  description="Build a landscaping estimate from service quantities and unit costs. Add shared delivery, overhead, and your target margin to calculate a project price."
  eyebrow="Free estimate calculator"
  h1="Landscaping Estimate Calculator"
  intro="Build a project from individual services and quantities. Enter your direct cost per service unit, add shared project expenses once, and calculate the price your margin requires."
  breadcrumbLabel="Landscaping Estimate Calculator"
  currentHref="/landscaping-estimate-calculator/"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <ServiceEstimateCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="extra">
    <article class="tool-editorial mb-10">
      <h2>Worked example: two services, one project overhead</h2>
      <p>Eight yards of mulch installation at a $75 direct unit cost contribute $600. Eighteen shrub installations at $40 direct cost each add $720. With $150 shared delivery, direct project cost is $1,470. Applying 15% overhead gives $1,690.50, and a 35% margin requires $2,600.77 before sales tax.</p>
      <p>These unit costs are examples, not recommended rates. Build your own using supplier prices, material quantities, paid crew time, and equipment needs. The <a href="/mulch-cost-calculator/">mulch calculator</a>, <a href="/topsoil-cost-calculator/">topsoil calculator</a>, and <a href="/landscape-labor-cost-calculator/">loaded labor calculator</a> can help with those inputs.</p>
      <p>Do not enter a selling rate as a direct cost: that would add overhead and profit to a price that already contains them. Likewise, if a service unit cost includes its own delivery allocation, omit that portion from shared delivery. Use the <a href="/landscape-profit-margin-calculator/">profit margin calculator</a> to review a final customer price, and the <a href="/landscape-job-cost-calculator/">job cost calculator</a> for the completed-job comparison.</p>
    </article>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink sm:text-3xl">How this estimate calculator works</h2>
    <ol class="mt-6 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {[
        { step: "1", title: "Build service lines", desc: "Multiply quantities by your direct cost per unit, including materials, labor, and equipment." },
        { step: "2", title: "Apply overhead", desc: "Your overhead percentage is added on top to reach a true project cost." },
        { step: "3", title: "Set your target margin", desc: "Margin, not markup — the profit share of the final price, not of cost." },
        { step: "4", title: "Get your price", desc: "The required selling price updates instantly and rounds upward to the next cent." },
      ].map((item) => (
        <li class="list-none rounded-2xl border border-border bg-paper p-5">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-forest text-sm font-bold text-lime">{item.step}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-bold text-ink">{item.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-muted">{item.desc}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted">
      Once your price is set, put it in front of the customer with our <a href="/landscaping-estimate-template/" class="font-semibold text-forest underline">landscaping estimate template</a> —
      fill in the same numbers and print or save a clean, customer-ready estimate.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolPageLayout>
